    "result_text": "I've made the change, and all 4 acceptance tests pass in `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Half-to-even rounding:** live claim due now rounds half to even, so 1.025 becomes 1.02 and 1.035 becomes 1.04 (`due()` in `core/rates.service.ts`). The server rounds the same way when it freezes a figure at settlement (`ClaimService.due`). Claims that were already settled keep their stored figure.\n- **Per-claim figures:** I added `claimDue()` in `core/claims.service.ts`. It returns the frozen figure for a settled claim, or the live due using the rate in force on the claim's date. The claim row and the due-totals both use it, so the two can't disagree.\n- **Due-totals** (`features/people/people.ts`):\n  - A person's due-total is now the sum of the rounded figures of their open and settled claims, and 0.00 if nothing counts.\n  - If their grade has no rate today, it shows n/a, unless one of their counting claims is settled with a frozen figure. In that case it's the sum of the figures there are.\n  - The sheet's due-total is still everyone's due-totals added up, leaving out anyone at n/a.\n\n**A choice the request didn't settle:** an open claim dated before any rate for its grade has no figure (it shows n/a). It adds nothing to its person's due-total rather than turning the whole total into n/a.\n\nI didn't change the stored data, so there's no new migration. The old migration that froze figures for already-settled claims rounded half up, and its comment still says so; I left that as it is.",
